  "en": {
   "stanzas": [
    [
     "William of Nassau",
     "am I, of Dutch blood;",
     "faithful to the fatherland",
     "I remain until death.",
     "A Prince of Orange",
     "am I, free, unafraid;",
     "the King of Spain",
     "I have always honoured."
    ],
    [
     "To live in the fear of God",
     "I have always striven;",
     "therefore I am driven out,",
     "bereft of land, of people.",
     "But God will govern me",
     "as a good instrument,",
     "so that I shall return",
     "into my rule."
    ],
    [
     "Bear it patiently, my subjects,",
     "who are upright by nature;",
     "God will not forsake you,",
     "though you are now burdened.",
     "Whoever wishes to live piously,",
     "let him pray to God night and day",
     "that He will give me strength,",
     "that I may help you."
    ],
    [
     "Life and goods all together",
     "I have not spared for you;",
     "my brothers, high of name,",
     "have also shown it to you:",
     "Count Adolf has fallen",
     "in Friesland, in the battle;",
     "his soul in eternal life",
     "awaits the Last Day."
    ],
    [
     "Noble and high-born,",
     "of imperial stock,",
     "chosen a prince of the Empire,",
     "as a pious Christian man,",
     "praised for God's word,",
     "I have, free and undaunted,",
     "as a hero without fear",
     "ventured my noble blood."
    ],
    [
     "My shield and my trust",
     "are You, O God my Lord;",
     "on You I will build,",
     "forsake me nevermore.",
     "That I may yet remain pious,",
     "your servant at every hour,",
     "and drive out the tyranny",
     "that wounds me through my heart."
    ],
    [
     "From all who burden me",
     "and are my persecutors,",
     "my God, be pleased to keep",
     "your faithful servant,",
     "that they do not take me by surprise",
     "in their wicked intent,",
     "do not wash their hands",
     "in my innocent blood."
    ],
    [
     "As David had to flee",
     "before Saul the tyrant,",
     "so I have had to sigh",
     "as many a nobleman.",
     "But God has raised him up,",
     "delivered him from all distress,",
     "given him a kingdom",
     "in Israel, very great."
    ],
    [
     "After the sour I shall receive",
     "from God my Lord the sweet;",
     "for that so longs",
     "my princely heart:",
     "that is, that I may die",
     "with honour on the field,",
     "and win an eternal kingdom",
     "as a faithful hero."
    ],
    [
     "Nothing moves me more to pity",
     "in my adversity",
     "than that one sees impoverished",
     "the King's good lands.",
     "That the Spaniards wrong you,",
     "O noble, sweet Netherland,",
     "when I think of it,",
     "my noble heart, it bleeds."
    ],
    [
     "As a prince on horseback",
     "with the strength of my army,",
     "from the arrogant tyrant",
     "I awaited the battle;",
     "he, dug in by Maastricht,",
     "feared my force;",
     "my horsemen were seen riding",
     "most boldly through the field."
    ],
    [
     "If it had been the will of the Lord",
     "at that time,",
     "I would gladly have turned away",
     "from you this heavy tempest.",
     "But the Lord from up above,",
     "who rules all things,",
     "whom one must always praise,",
     "did not desire it."
    ],
    [
     "Very Christian was the drive",
     "of my princely heart;",
     "steadfast has remained",
     "my heart in adversity.",
     "The Lord I have prayed",
     "from the bottom of my heart",
     "that He will save my cause,",
     "make my innocence known."
    ],
    [
     "Farewell, my poor sheep,",
     "who are in great distress;",
     "your shepherd will not sleep,",
     "though you are now scattered.",
     "Turn to God,",
     "take up his saving word,",
     "live as pious Christians,-",
     "it will soon be over here."
    ],
    [
     "Before God I will confess,",
     "and before his great might,",
     "that at no time",
     "have I despised the King,",
     "except that God the Lord,",
     "the highest Majesty,",
     "I have had to obey",
     "in righteousness."
    ]
   ],
